      excerpt: 'Seven stories from the last day: a 20-plus-signatory open letter fronted by Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang’s first-ever X post argues distillation is a "natural process" not theft, ~200 venture-backed startups separately urge the White House not to block Chinese open-weight models, 21 APEC economies including the US and China adopt a joint statement backing open-source AI, Anthropic ships Claude Opus 5 at half the price of frontier intelligence, a researcher discloses a since-mitigated sandbox escape in Claude Cowork that exposed host Mac credentials, a Nikkei Asia investigation finds Big Tech is carrying $1.65T in off-balance-sheet AI debt, and Intel posts its fastest revenue growth in 15 years on AI-driven demand.',
